<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n4623" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">austrālis</span></b> , e, adj.
		1.auster, II., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>southern</i> (syn.: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">austrinus, meridianus): quae (regio) tum est
					aquilonia tum australis, Cic N D. 2, 19, 50: cingulus,</span>”
				i. e. <i>the torrid zone</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">id. Rep. 6, 20, 21</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">ora, the same,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. Tusc. 1, 28, 68</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">plaga,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">Vulg.
					Gen. 13, 11</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">terra,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. ib. 24, 62</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">pars,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">ib. Exod 40, 32</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">polus,</span>”
				<i>the south pole</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Ov. M.
					2, 132</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">nimbi,</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">id. P 4, 4, 1</span></i>
			: 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">annus,</span>”
				<i>Egyptian</i>,
				 <i><span class="en">Claud. Eutr. 1, 403</span></i>
			.</div>
